const navItems=[['Dashboard','⌂'],['Dataset','▤'],['Data Warehouse','▦'],['OLAP Analysis','◷'],['Classification','◉'],['Customer Segmentation','◌'],['Association Rules','⇄'],['Next Product Prediction','➜']];let page='Dashboard',summary=null,samplePage=1,sampleSize=12,sampleTotal=0,sampleSort='CustomerID',sampleDir='asc',sampleSearch='',schemaData=null,activeTable='FACT_CUSTOMER_ACTIVITY',selectedCustomer=null,cluster=0,associationThreshold={support:0.10,confidence:0.50},olapState={mode:"rollup",level:"month",gender:"",fit:"",location:"",year:"",period:"",rows:"Product_Fit_Category",cols:"Next_Product_Uptake",measure:"customers"};
const $=s=>document.querySelector(s),esc=s=>String(s??'').replace(/[&<>"']/g,c=>({'&':'&amp;','<':'&lt;','>':'&gt;','"':'&quot;',"'":'&#39;'}[c])),fmt=(n,d=0)=>Number(n||0).toLocaleString('en-IN',{maximumFractionDigits:d}),money=n=>'₹'+fmt(n,0),pct=n=>(Number(n||0)*100).toFixed(1)+'%',cap=s=>String(s||'').replaceAll('_',' '),api=async p=>{let r=await fetch('/api'+p);let j=await r.json();if(!r.ok)throw Error(j.error||'Request failed');return j};
function chartBars(items,{key='name',value='value',color='#3479de',format=v=>fmt(v),height=205,aspect='none'}={}){if(!items?.length)return '<div class="empty">No data for this selection</div>';let W=600,H=height,L=200,R=48,T=8,B=20,inner=H-T-B,row=(inner/items.length),max=Math.max(1,...items.map(d=>+d[value]||0));return `<svg class="chart" style="height:${height}px" viewBox="0 0 ${W} ${H}" preserveAspectRatio="${aspect}" role="img">${items.map((d,i)=>{let y=T+i*row+row*.25,bw=(W-L-R)*(+d[value]||0)/max,label=String(d[key]),labelText=label.length>25?label.slice(0,24)+'…':label,fit=labelText.length*8>L-18;return `<text x="${L-10}" y="${y+row*.42}" text-anchor="end" font-size="13" font-family="Arial,sans-serif" fill="#9eb2c6" ${fit?`textLength="${L-20}" lengthAdjust="spacingAndGlyphs"`:''}>${esc(labelText)}</text><rect x="${L}" y="${y}" width="${Math.max(1,bw)}" height="${Math.max(6,row*.48)}" rx="4" fill="${color}" opacity="${.9-i*.035}"/><text x="${L+bw+6}" y="${y+row*.40}" font-size="13" font-family="Arial,sans-serif" fill="#c4d3e0">${esc(format(d[value]))}</text>`}).join('')}</svg>`}
function pivotChartBars(items,{height=300}={}){if(!items?.length)return '<div class="empty">No data for this selection</div>';let W=600,H=height,L=305,R=48,T=8,B=20,inner=H-T-B,row=inner/items.length,max=Math.max(1,...items.map(d=>+d.value||0));return `<svg class="chart" style="height:${height}px" viewBox="0 0 ${W} ${H}" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet" role="img">${items.map((d,i)=>{let y=T+i*row+row*.25,bw=(W-L-R)*(+d.value||0)/max,[first,second]=String(d.period).split(' · '),label=`${first} → ${second||''}`,fit=label.length*6.5>L-18;return `<text x="${L-10}" y="${y+row*.48}" text-anchor="end" font-size="11" font-family="Arial,sans-serif" fill="#9eb2c6" ${fit?`textLength="${L-18}" lengthAdjust="spacingAndGlyphs"`:''}>${esc(label)}</text><rect x="${L}" y="${y+row*.12}" width="${Math.max(1,bw)}" height="${Math.max(6,row*.48)}" rx="4" fill="#3479de" opacity="${.9-i*.035}"/><text x="${L+bw+6}" y="${y+row*.48}" font-size="13" font-family="Arial,sans-serif" fill="#c4d3e0">${fmt(d.value)}</text>`}).join('')}</svg>`}
function barShares(items){let max=Math.max(.01,...items.map(x=>x.share));return items.map(x=>`<div class="bar-row"><span>${esc(x.name)}</span><div class="bar-track"><div class="bar-fill" style="width:${x.share/max*100}%"></div></div><b>${pct(x.share)}</b></div>`).join('')}
function kpi(label,value,note,icon='◈'){return `<div class="kpi"><span class="kpi-icon">${icon}</span><div class="kpi-label">${label}</div><div class="kpi-value">${value}</div><div class="kpi-note">${note}</div></div>`}
function head(title,sub,eyebrow='ANALYTICS'){return `<div class="page-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">${eyebrow}</div><h1 class="page-title">${title}</h1><p class="page-sub">${sub}</p></div></div>`}
function card(title,sub,body,tag=''){return `<section class="card"><div class="card-head"><div><div class="card-title">${title}</div>${sub?`<div class="card-sub">${sub}</div>`:''}</div>${tag?`<span class="tag">${tag}</span>`:''}</div>${body}</section>`}
function table(headers,rows){return `<div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr>${headers.map(h=>`<th>${h}</th>`).join('')}</tr></thead><tbody>${rows||''}</tbody></table></div>`}
function pageTitle(){ $('#crumb').textContent=page;document.querySelectorAll('nav button').forEach(b=>b.classList.toggle('active',b.dataset.page===page));}
async function render(){pageTitle();let app=$('#app');app.innerHTML='<div class="empty">Loading analytical data…</div>';try{if(!summary)summary=await api('/dataset/summary');let html=page==='Dashboard'?await dashboard():page==='Dataset'?await dataset():page==='Data Warehouse'?await warehouse():page==='OLAP Analysis'?await olap():page==='Classification'?await modelPage(false):page==='Next Product Prediction'?await modelPage(true):page==='Customer Segmentation'?await clustering():await association();app.innerHTML=html;if(page==='Association Rules'){let t=document.querySelector('#rules-table');t?.closest('section').insertAdjacentHTML('beforebegin',networkMarkup()+card('Support vs confidence','Each bubble is a live rule; bubble size follows lift.',associationScatter(window.currentRules||[]),'ACTUAL CUSTOMER FLAGS'))}bindPage()}catch(e){app.innerHTML=`<div class="card"><h2>Dashboard data unavailable</h2><p class="page-sub">${esc(e.message)}. Confirm the local server is running and try again.</p></div>`}}
async function dashboard(){let bench=await api('/mining/benchmarks'),prod=summary.products.slice().sort((a,b)=>b.share-a.share),fits=Object.entries(summary.fit).map(([name,value])=>({name:cap(name),value}));return `${head('Bank Customer Segmentation','Data Warehouse & Data Mining Analytics','PROJECT OVERVIEW')}<div class="grid kpis">${kpi('CUSTOMERS',fmt(summary.customers),'Customer-level analytical rows','♙')}${kpi('ATTRIBUTES',fmt(summary.attributes),'Cleaned analytical dataset','▤')}${kpi('TOTAL TRANSACTION AMOUNT',money(summary.totalAmount),'Aggregated customer activity','↗')}${kpi('AVERAGE ACCOUNT BALANCE',money(summary.avgBalance),'Per customer','₹')}${kpi('AVERAGE TRANSACTION AMOUNT',money(summary.avgAmount),'Per customer snapshot','₹')}${kpi('ACTIVE PRODUCTS',fmt(summary.products.length),'Derived ownership indicators','▧')}</div><div class="grid cols2" style="margin-bottom:16px">${card('Product ownership','Share of customers owning each derived product',barShares(prod))}${card('Product fit distribution','Derived customer-product fit labels',chartBars(fits,{key:'name',value:'value',color:'#22a2b4'}))}</div><div class="grid cols3" style="margin-bottom:16px">${card('Project benchmark · Classification','Random Forest · stated project result',`<div class="metric-band"><div class="metric"><b>98.2%</b><small>Accuracy</small></div><div class="metric"><b>0.982</b><small>Macro F1</small></div></div><p class="footnote">Established project benchmark; not recomputed by this dashboard.</p>`)}${card('Project benchmark · Next product','Random Forest · stated project result',`<div class="metric-band"><div class="metric"><b>97.7%</b><small>Accuracy</small></div><div class="metric"><b>0.973</b><small>Macro F1</small></div></div><p class="footnote">Established project benchmark; not recomputed by this dashboard.</p>`)}${card('Project benchmark · Clustering','K-Means · stated project result',`<div class="kpi-value">K = 5</div><div class="card-sub">${bench.clustering.sizes.map(fmt).join(' · ')} customers across five clusters</div><p class="footnote">Cluster membership is not independently recomputed.</p>`)}</div><div class="grid cols2">${card('Data pipeline','From raw transaction source to mining outputs',`<div class="method-grid"><div class="method-step"><b>01 · Raw source</b><small>1,048,567 transaction rows</small></div><div class="method-step"><b>02 · ETL</b><small>Clean, validate & aggregate</small></div><div class="method-step"><b>03 · Warehouse</b><small>Star schema snapshot grain</small></div><div class="method-step"><b>04 · Analytics</b><small>OLAP and data mining</small></div></div>`)}${card('Strongest benchmark association','Co-occurrence, not causation',`<div class="rule-highlight"><b>Personal Loan → Credit Card</b><div class="metric-band" style="margin-top:13px"><div class="metric"><b>0.166</b><small>Support</small></div><div class="metric"><b>0.577</b><small>Confidence</small></div><div class="metric"><b>1.884</b><small>Lift</small></div></div></div>`)}</div><div class="spacer"></div><div class="notice"><strong>Data interpretation.</strong> The cleaned CSV contains one row per customer with aggregated activity. Product ownership, Product Fit Category, and Next Product Uptake are derived analytical attributes, not fields from the raw transaction source.</div>`}
async function dataset(){let d=await api(`/dataset/sample?page=${samplePage}&size=${sampleSize}&sort=${encodeURIComponent(sampleSort)}&dir=${sampleDir}&search=${encodeURIComponent(sampleSearch)}`);sampleTotal=d.total;let cols=d.columns;let visible=['CustomerID','Age','CustGender','CustLocation','Account_Balance','Transaction_Count','Total_Transaction_Amount_INR','Activity_Days','Financial_Activity_Score','Product_Fit_Category','Next_Product_Uptake'];let rows=d.rows.map(r=>`<tr>${visible.map(c=>`<td>${esc(['Account_Balance','Total_Transaction_Amount_INR'].includes(c)?money(r[c]):c==='Financial_Activity_Score'?Number(r[c]).toFixed(3):r[c])}</td>`).join('')}</tr>`).join('');return `${head('Dataset','Customer-level analytical data: searchable, sortable, paginated and computed from the provided CSV.','DATA EXPLORER')}<div class="grid kpis">${kpi('CUSTOMERS',fmt(summary.customers),'Rows in analytical file')}${kpi('ATTRIBUTES',fmt(summary.attributes),'Columns in analytical file')}${kpi('DOMAIN',summary.domain,'Data subject area')}${kpi('GRANULARITY',summary.granularity,'One row per customer')}</div><div class="grid cols2" style="margin-bottom:16px">${card('Financial statistics','Calculated across all 20,000 customers',`<div class="metric-band">${[['Average balance',money(summary.avgBalance)],['Average transaction amount',money(summary.avgAmount)],['Average transaction count',fmt(summary.avgTxCount,2)],['Average activity days',fmt(summary.avgDays,1)],['Financial activity score',fmt(summary.avgScore,3)]].map(([a,b])=>`<div class="metric"><b>${b}</b><small>${a}</small></div>`).join('')}</div><p class="footnote">Total transaction amount: ${money(summary.totalAmount)} across customer aggregates.</p>`)}${card('Derived product ownership','Percentage of customers with each ownership flag',barShares(summary.products))}</div><div class="grid cols2" style="margin-bottom:16px">${card('Product Fit Category','Actual cleaned dataset distribution',chartBars(Object.entries(summary.fit).map(([name,value])=>({name:cap(name),value}))))}${card('Next Product Uptake','Actual cleaned dataset distribution',chartBars(Object.entries(summary.uptake).map(([name,value])=>({name:cap(name),value})),{color:'#1aa5b8'}))}</div>${card('Dataset sample','Showing 12 records per page; all columns are sortable via column headings.',`<div class="toolbar"><input class="input search" id="sample-search" placeholder="Search CustomerID…" value="${esc(sampleSearch)}"><span class="muted">${fmt(d.total)} matching customers</span><select class="select" id="sample-size"><option value="12" ${sampleSize===12?'selected':''}>12 per page</option><option value="25" ${sampleSize===25?'selected':''}>25 per page</option></select></div>${table(visible.map(c=>`<span data-sort="${c}">${c.replaceAll('_',' ')}</span>`),rows)}<div class="table-foot"><span>Page ${d.page} of ${Math.max(1,Math.ceil(d.total/d.size))}</span><div class="pager"><button id="prev">← Previous</button><button id="next">Next →</button></div></div>`)}<div class="spacer"></div>${card('Data quality & source coverage','Programmatic checks performed against the provided files',`<div class="metric-band"><div class="metric"><b>0</b><small>Missing analytical cells</small></div><div class="metric"><b>0</b><small>Duplicate customer rows</small></div><div class="metric"><b>${fmt(summary.locations)}</b><small>Unique locations</small></div><div class="metric"><b>${fmt(summary.etl.rawRows)}</b><small>Raw transaction records</small></div></div><p class="footnote">Original ZIP structure: one CSV with 9 columns. Raw source dates: ${summary.etl.dateMin}–${summary.etl.dateMax}; ${fmt(summary.etl.matchedCustomers)} of ${fmt(summary.customers)} analytical customers matched by CustomerID. The supplied cleaned CSV has 21 headers; the dashboard reports the inspected file.</p>`)}`}
async function warehouse(){schemaData=await api('/warehouse/schema');let names=Object.keys(schemaData.schema),cards=names.map(n=>{let f=n.startsWith('FACT');return `<div class="schema-table ${f?'fact':'dim'} ${n===activeTable?'selected':''}" data-table="${n}" tabindex="0" role="button" aria-label="Inspect ${n}"><div class="st-head">${f?'◆':'◇'} &nbsp;${n}</div>${schemaData.schema[n].columns.slice(0,f?8:5).map(c=>`<div class="st-col">${c.replace('(PK)','<b class="pk">(PK)</b>').replace('(FK)','<b class="fk">(FK)</b>')}</div>`).join('')}${schemaData.schema[n].columns.length>(f?8:5)?'<div class="st-col muted">… more columns</div>':''}</div>`}).join('');let s=schemaData.schema[activeTable];return `${head('Data Warehouse','Customer snapshot warehouse modeled as a fact table surrounded by descriptive dimensions.','STAR SCHEMA')}<div class="notice"><strong>Fact grain:</strong> ${schemaData.grain} The original transaction data supplies last-recorded-date information; it is not the fact table grain.</div><div class="card" style="margin-top:16px"><div class="card-head"><div><div class="card-title">Interactive star schema</div><div class="card-sub">Select a table to inspect its purpose, columns and relationships. Hover to explore the 3D model.</div></div><span class="tag">3 dimensions · 1 fact</span></div><div class="schema-scene"><div class="schema">${cards}<svg class="schema-links" viewBox="0 0 1000 520" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true"><defs><marker id="schema-arrow" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" refX="7" refY="4" orient="auto"><path d="M0,0 L8,4 L0,8z" fill="#43c4d3"/></marker></defs><path d="M165 190 C165 210 405 210 450 225"/><path d="M500 190 L500 225"/><path d="M835 190 C835 210 595 210 550 225"/></svg></div></div><div class="legend"><span style="--dot:#3b80dc">Fact table</span><span style="--dot:#a4b9cc">Dimension table</span><span style="--dot:#2674ca">Primary key</span><span style="--dot:#1b9aab">Foreign key</span></div></div><div class="schema-details" style="margin-top:16px">${card(s?activeTable:'Table',s?.purpose||'',`<div class="metric-band"><div class="metric"><b>${s?.pk||'—'}</b><small>Primary key</small></div><div class="metric"><b style="font-size:11px">${s?.fk||'—'}</b><small>Foreign keys</small></div></div><div class="spacer"></div><div class="detail-list">${(s?.columns||[]).map(c=>`<span class="pill">${c}</span>`).join('')}</div>`)}${card('ETL source validation','Original transaction CSV inside supplied ZIP',`<div class="metric-band"><div class="metric"><b>${fmt(schemaData.raw.rows)}</b><small>Transaction rows</small></div><div class="metric"><b>${fmt(schemaData.raw.customers)}</b><small>Distinct raw customers</small></div><div class="metric"><b>${fmt(schemaData.raw.dateMin.slice(0,4))}–${fmt(schemaData.raw.dateMax.slice(0,4))}</b><small>Source date range</small></div><div class="metric"><b>${fmt(schemaData.dates.length)}</b><small>Snapshot dates</small></div></div><p class="footnote">The 20,000 analytical CustomerIDs all matched the source transaction data. The customer dataset contains aggregated fields and derived labels not present in the raw CSV.</p>`)}</div><div class="spacer"></div>${card('Methodology & limitations','Interpretation notes for project evaluation',`<div class="method-grid"><div class="method-step"><b>Derived labels</b><small>Product ownership, Product Fit, and Next Product are derived analytical attributes.</small></div><div class="method-step"><b>Validation</b><small>Random train-test split is not a substitute for time-based validation.</small></div><div class="method-step"><b>Clustering</b><small>K = 5 is presented as the stated practical choice for separation and interpretation.</small></div><div class="method-step"><b>Association</b><small>Rules represent co-occurrence and do not establish causation.</small></div></div>`)}`}
function olapCube(state,summary,filters,data){let x=state.mode==='pivot'?cap(state.rows):(['rollup','drilldown'].includes(state.mode)?'Date · '+state.level[0].toUpperCase()+state.level.slice(1):'Gender');let y=state.mode==='pivot'?cap(state.cols):(['rollup','drilldown'].includes(state.mode)?'Product Fit':'Location');let z=state.mode==='pivot'?(state.measure==='customers'?'Customer Count':cap(state.measure)):'Customer Count';let active=Object.entries(filters).filter(([,v])=>v).map(([k,v])=>cap(k).replace(/^./,c=>c.toUpperCase())+': '+cap(v));if(state.period)active.push('Date: '+state.period);let chips=active.length?active.map(x=>'<span class="cube-chip">'+esc(x)+'</span>').join(''):'<span class="cube-chip">All customers</span>';return '<section class="olap-cube-panel" aria-label="Live OLAP cube"><div class="cube-heading"><div><b>Live OLAP cube</b><small>Warehouse dimensions and active slice</small></div><span class="cube-mode">'+esc(data.operation)+'</span></div><div class="cube-scene"><div class="cube" data-operation="'+esc(state.mode)+'"><div class="cube-face cube-front"><small>X AXIS</small><strong>'+esc(x)+'</strong><b>'+fmt(summary.customers)+'</b><span>customers</span></div><div class="cube-face cube-top"><small>Y AXIS</small><strong>'+esc(y)+'</strong><b>'+money(summary.totalAmount)+'</b><span>total amount</span></div><div class="cube-face cube-right"><small>Z AXIS</small><strong>'+esc(z)+'</strong><b>'+esc(state.mode==='pivot'?'PIVOT':state.mode.toUpperCase())+'</b><span>active measure</span></div><div class="cube-face cube-back"></div><div class="cube-face cube-left"></div><div class="cube-face cube-bottom"></div></div></div><div class="cube-filter-label">Current filters</div><div class="cube-filters">'+chips+'</div></section>'}
async function olap(){
 const state={...olapState};
 const filters=state.mode==='slice'?(()=>{const first=['gender','location','fit','year'].find(k=>state[k]);return first?{[first]:state[first]}:{}})():{gender:state.gender,location:state.location,fit:state.fit,year:state.year};
 const q=new URLSearchParams({level:state.level,...filters,period:state.mode==='drilldown'?state.period:''});
 if(state.mode==='pivot'){q.set('rows',state.rows);q.set('cols',state.cols);q.set('measure',state.measure)}
 const data=await api('/olap/'+state.mode+'?'+q),rows=data.rows||[];
 const bars=state.mode==='pivot'?rows.flatMap(r=>data.columns.map(c=>({period:`${cap(r.row)} · ${cap(c)}`,value:r[c]}))).sort((a,b)=>b.value-a.value).slice(0,10):rows.map(r=>({period:r.period,value:r.totalAmount})).sort((a,b)=>b.value-a.value).slice(0,12);
 const chart=state.mode==='pivot'?pivotChartBars(bars,{height:Math.max(250,bars.length*30)}):chartBars(bars,{key:'period',value:'value',height:250,aspect:'xMidYMid meet',format:money});
 const resultTable=state.mode==='pivot'?table(['Row · '+cap(data.rowDimension),...data.columns.map(cap)],rows.map(r=>`<tr><td>${esc(r.row)}</td>${data.columns.map(c=>`<td>${fmt(r[c],state.measure==='customers'?0:2)}</td>`).join('')}</tr>`).join('')):table(['Period / Product Fit','Customers','Total snapshot amount','Avg transaction','Avg balance','Avg activity score'],rows.map(r=>`<tr><td>${['rollup','drilldown'].includes(state.mode)&&state.level!=='day'?`<button class="btn period-drill" data-period="${esc(r.period)}">${esc(r.period)} ↘</button>`:esc(cap(r.period))}</td><td>${fmt(r.customers)}</td><td>${money(r.totalAmount)}</td><td>${money(r.avgAmount)}</td><td>${money(r.avgBalance)}</td><td>${fmt(r.avgScore,3)}</td></tr>`).join(''));
 return `${head('OLAP Analysis','Work with real customer snapshot data. Choose a time hierarchy, filter dimensions, and pivot measures.','MULTIDIMENSIONAL ANALYSIS')}<div class="notice"><strong>Warehouse measure:</strong> transaction totals and other financial measures are customer-level aggregates grouped by each customer’s last recorded transaction date. The fact grain remains one snapshot per customer.</div><div class="card olap-console" style="margin-top:16px"><div class="toolbar olap-filter-controls"><label class="olap-control"><span>Operation</span><select class="select" id="olap-mode"><option value="rollup" ${state.mode==='rollup'?'selected':''}>Roll-Up</option><option value="drilldown" ${state.mode==='drilldown'?'selected':''}>Drill-Down</option><option value="slice" ${state.mode==='slice'?'selected':''}>Slice</option><option value="dice" ${state.mode==='dice'?'selected':''}>Dice</option><option value="pivot" ${state.mode==='pivot'?'selected':''}>Pivot</option></select></label><label class="olap-control"><span>Time level</span><select class="select" id="olap-level">${['day','month','quarter','year'].map(x=>`<option value="${x}" ${state.level===x?'selected':''}>${x[0].toUpperCase()+x.slice(1)}</option>`).join('')}</select></label><label class="olap-control"><span>Gender</span><select class="select" id="olap-gender"><option value="" ${!state.gender?'selected':''}>All</option><option value="M" ${state.gender==='M'?'selected':''}>Male</option><option value="F" ${state.gender==='F'?'selected':''}>Female</option><option value="Unknown" ${state.gender==='Unknown'?'selected':''}>Unknown</option></select></label><label class="olap-control"><span>Location</span><select class="select" id="olap-location"><option value="" ${!state.location?'selected':''}>All locations</option>${summary.topLocations.map(x=>`<option value="${esc(x.name)}" ${state.location===x.name?'selected':''}>${esc(x.name)}</option>`).join('')}</select></label><label class="olap-control"><span>Product Fit</span><select class="select" id="olap-fit"><option value="" ${!state.fit?'selected':''}>All categories</option>${Object.keys(summary.fit).map(x=>`<option value="${esc(x)}" ${state.fit===x?'selected':''}>${esc(cap(x))}</option>`).join('')}</select></label><label class="olap-control"><span>Year</span><select class="select" id="olap-year"><option value="" ${!state.year?'selected':''}>All years</option><option value="2016" ${state.year==='2016'?'selected':''}>2016</option></select></label><button class="btn" id="olap-reset">Reset</button></div><div class="toolbar pivot-controls"><label class="olap-control"><span>Pivot rows</span><select class="select" id="pivot-rows">${[['CustLocation','Location'],['Product_Fit_Category','Product Fit'],['Year','Year'],['CustGender','Gender']].map(([v,n])=>`<option value="${v}" ${state.rows===v?'selected':''}>${n}</option>`).join('')}</select></label><label class="olap-control"><span>Columns</span><select class="select" id="pivot-cols">${[['Product_Fit_Category','Product Fit'],['CustGender','Gender'],['Next_Product_Uptake','Next Product'],['CustLocation','Location']].map(([v,n])=>`<option value="${v}" ${state.cols===v?'selected':''}>${n}</option>`).join('')}</select></label><label class="olap-control"><span>Measure</span><select class="select" id="pivot-measure">${[['customers','Customer Count'],['Transaction_Count','Transaction Count'],['Total_Transaction_Amount_INR','Total Transaction Amount'],['Average_Transaction_Amount_INR','Average Transaction Amount'],['Account_Balance','Average Account Balance'],['Financial_Activity_Score','Average Financial Activity Score']].map(([v,n])=>`<option value="${v}" ${state.measure===v?'selected':''}>${n}</option>`).join('')}</select></label><button class="btn primary" id="run-pivot">Apply Pivot</button></div><div class="card-head"><div><div class="card-title">Active operation · ${esc(data.operation)}</div><div class="card-sub">${state.mode==='slice'?'Slice applies the first selected dimension filter.':state.mode==='dice'?'Dice combines every selected dimension filter.':state.mode==='pivot'?`Rows: ${cap(data.rowDimension)} · Columns: ${cap(data.columnDimension)} · Measure: ${state.measure==='customers'?'Customer Count':cap(state.measure)}`:`${state.mode==='rollup'?'Roll-up':'Drill-down'} by ${state.level}; change level to move through Day → Month → Quarter → Year.`}</div></div><span class="tag">${fmt(data.summary.customers)} customers</span></div><div class="grid cols2"><div><div class="card-sub">${state.mode==='pivot'?`Top ${bars.length} pivot combinations by ${state.measure==='customers'?'customer count':cap(state.measure)} · full pivot table below`:(state.level==='day'?'Top 12 daily amounts · full date table below':'Total transaction amount by period · chart shows up to 12 groups')}</div>${chart}</div><div class="olap-insights">${olapCube(state,data.summary,filters,data)}<div class="metric-band">${[['Customers',fmt(data.summary.customers)],['Total amount',money(data.summary.totalAmount)],['Average balance',money(data.summary.avgBalance)],['Mean transaction count',fmt(data.summary.avgTxCount,2)]].map(([a,b])=>`<div class="metric"><b>${b}</b><small>${a}</small></div>`).join('')}</div></div></div><div class="spacer"></div>${rows.length?resultTable:'<div class="empty">No matching customers for these filters. Reset or broaden the selection.</div>'}<p class="footnote">Roll-up and drill-down aggregate by the customer’s source-derived snapshot date. Slice and dice recalculate summary metrics on the filtered customer subset. Pivot rebuilds its table and chart on the server.</p></div>`
}function matrixView(matrix,classes){let max=Math.max(...matrix.flat());return `<div class="matrix" style="grid-template-columns:150px repeat(${classes.length},minmax(54px,1fr))"><div class="matrix-label">Actual ↓ / Predicted →</div>${classes.map(c=>`<div class="matrix-label" title="${esc(c)}">${esc(cap(c))}</div>`).join('')}${matrix.map((row,i)=>`<div class="matrix-row" style="display:contents"><div class="matrix-label" title="${esc(classes[i])}">${esc(cap(classes[i]))}</div>${row.map(v=>`<div class="heat-cell" title="${fmt(v)} records" style="background:rgba(42,131,226,${.12+.82*(v/max)});color:${v/max>.58?'#f5fbff':'#bddaf6'}">${fmt(v)}</div>`).join('')}</div>`).join('')}</div>`}
function featureBars(items){let max=Math.max(...items.map(x=>x[1]));return `<div class="feature-list">${items.map(([n,v])=>`<div class="feature-line"><span title="${esc(n)}">${esc(cap(n))}</span><div class="bar-track"><div class="bar-fill" style="width:${Math.max(2,100*v/max)}%"></div></div><b>${(100*v).toFixed(1)}%</b></div>`).join('')}</div>`}
function modelCompareChart(items){const W=620,H=238,L=178,R=22,T=18,B=28,row=(H-T-B)/items.length,plot=W-L-R,ticks=[0,.25,.5,.75,1],grid=ticks.map(v=>'<line x1="'+(L+plot*v)+'" y1="'+T+'" x2="'+(L+plot*v)+'" y2="'+(H-B)+'" class="model-gridline"/><text x="'+(L+plot*v)+'" y="'+(H-7)+'" text-anchor="middle" class="model-tick">'+Math.round(v*100)+'%</text>').join(''),bars=items.map((d,i)=>{const y=T+i*row+row*.2,bw1=plot*Math.max(0,Math.min(1,d.accuracy)),bw2=plot*Math.max(0,Math.min(1,d.macroF1));return '<text x="'+(L-12)+'" y="'+(y+row*.45)+'" text-anchor="end" class="model-label">'+esc(d.model)+'</text><rect x="'+L+'" y="'+y+'" width="'+bw1+'" height="12" rx="4" fill="#438df2"/><text x="'+(L+bw1+5)+'" y="'+(y+10)+'" class="model-value">'+pct(d.accuracy)+'</text><rect x="'+L+'" y="'+(y+16)+'" width="'+bw2+'" height="12" rx="4" fill="#20b8c7"/><text x="'+(L+bw2+5)+'" y="'+(y+26)+'" class="model-value">'+pct(d.macroF1)+'</text>'}).join('');return '<div class="model-chart-wrap"><svg class="model-compare-chart" viewBox="0 0 '+W+' '+H+'" role="img" aria-label="Accuracy and macro F1 comparison across models">'+grid+bars+'</svg><div class="model-chart-legend"><span><i style="--model-color:#438df2"></i>Accuracy</span><span><i style="--model-color:#20b8c7"></i>Macro F1</span></div></div>'}
async function modelPage(pred){let [bench,data]=await Promise.all([api('/mining/benchmarks'),api('/mining/results')]),m=pred?bench.prediction:bench.classification,out=pred?data.prediction:data.classification,target=pred?'Next_Product_Uptake':'Product_Fit_Category',title=pred?'Next Product Prediction':'Classification',comp=pred?data.modelComparison.prediction:data.modelComparison.classification,classes=out.classes;let compare=comp.map(x=>`<tr><td>${esc(x.model)}</td><td>${pct(x.accuracy)}</td><td>${pct(x.macroF1)}</td><td>${x.macroPrecision===undefined?'—':x.macroPrecision.toFixed(3)}</td><td>${x.macroRecall===undefined?'—':x.macroRecall.toFixed(3)}</td><td><span class="pill">${esc(x.status)}</span></td></tr>`).join('');let dist=Object.entries(pred?summary.uptake:summary.fit).map(([name,value])=>({name:cap(name),value}));return `${head(title,pred?'Random Forest estimates the next-product label from the customer profile.':'Predict the predefined product-fit category from financial and behavioural features.','SUPERVISED MINING')}<div class="notice"><strong>${pred?'Decision support:':'Classification objective:'}</strong> ${pred?'This is a model-based analytical prediction. It does not guarantee future customer behaviour.':'Classification predicts the predefined Product_Fit_Category. It is a derived analytical fit label, not an actual bank product.'} CustomerID, CustLocation, and both supervised targets are excluded from predictors according to the documented methodology.</div><div class="grid kpis" style="margin-top:16px">${kpi('PROJECT BENCHMARK',pct(m.accuracy),'Random Forest accuracy')}${kpi('MACRO F1',m.macroF1.toFixed(3),'Random Forest')}${kpi('MACRO PRECISION',m.macroPrecision.toFixed(3),'Random Forest')}${kpi('MACRO RECALL',m.macroRecall.toFixed(3),'Random Forest')}</div><div class="grid model-top-grid" style="margin-bottom:16px">${card('Model comparison','Stratified 80/20 holdout · random_state 42',`${table(['Model','Accuracy','Macro F1','Macro Precision','Macro Recall','Value status'],compare)}${modelCompareChart(comp)}<p class="source-note">Random Forest values are established benchmark metrics. Logistic Regression and Extra Trees comparison values are approximate readings; precision and recall were not reported for these models.</p>`)}${card(pred?'Observed target distribution':'Product-fit class distribution','Calculated from the provided analytical CSV',chartBars(dist,{key:'name',value:'value',color:'#35b6cc'}))}</div><div class="grid cols2" style="margin-bottom:16px">${card('Held-out confusion matrix','4,000-row test set · Random Forest',matrixView(out.confusionMatrix,classes),'TEST N=4,000')}${card('Permutation feature importance','Macro-F1 decrease when each feature is shuffled; chart-read values are approximate',featureBars(out.permutationImportance))}</div>${!pred?`<div class="grid cols2" style="margin-bottom:16px">${card('One-vs-rest ROC','Reported one-vs-rest AUC values',`<div class="metric-band">${out.rocAuc.map(x=>`<div class="metric"><b>${Number(x.auc).toFixed(2)}</b><small>${esc(cap(x.class))} AUC</small></div>`).join('')}</div><div class="source-note">ROC curves and labels are reproduced in the project evaluation figure below.</div>`)}${card('Evaluation and leakage checks','Project-reported setup',`<div class="method-grid"><div class="method-step"><b>Split</b><small>80% train / 20% test, stratified, seed 42.</small></div><div class="method-step"><b>Inputs</b><small>Numeric imputation/scaling and one-hot encoding.</small></div><div class="method-step"><b>Excluded</b><small>CustomerID, high-cardinality CustLocation and target columns.</small></div><div class="method-step"><b>Validation</b><small>Random split does not replace time-based validation.</small></div></div>`)}</div>`:''}<div class="grid cols2" style="margin-bottom:16px">${card('Project evaluation figure','Model evaluation',`<div class="visual-frame"><img class="visual-artifact" src="/assets/project/${pred?'prediction_diagnostics.png':'classification_diagnostics.png'}" alt="${pred?'Next-product confusion matrix and permutation importance':'Classification one-vs-rest ROC and permutation importance'}"></div><p class="source-note">These are recorded model evaluation outputs, not a new training run in this dashboard.</p>`)}${card(pred?'Prediction workflow':'Customer prediction lookup','CustomerID search loads the matching record from the analytical dataset.',`<div class="toolbar"><input id="customer-id" class="input search" placeholder="Enter a CustomerID"><button id="find-customer" class="btn primary">Find customer</button></div><div id="customer-result"><div class="empty">Search a customer to view their profile and recorded ${esc(target)} label.</div></div><p class="footnote">No fitted model file or per-customer probabilities are included with the project evaluations or datasets. The profile lookup shows the recorded analytical label, never a fabricated model prediction.</p>`)}</div><div class="spacer"></div>${card('Methodology & limitations','',`<div class="method-grid"><div class="method-step"><b>Targets</b><small>Product Fit and Next Product are derived fields; verify construction for leakage.</small></div><div class="method-step"><b>Validation</b><small>Random holdout results may not represent future periods.</small></div><div class="method-step"><b>Metrics</b><small>Accuracy and macro metrics are shown together because class balance differs.</small></div><div class="method-step"><b>Use</b><small>Prediction scores do not guarantee uptake or justify credit decisions.</small></div></div>`)}`}function clusterSelector(sizes,selected){return '<div class="interactive-row cluster-selector">'+sizes.map((n,i)=>'<button class="btn cluster-choice '+(selected===i?'active primary':'')+'" data-cluster="'+i+'">C'+i+' · '+pct(n/20000)+'</button>').join('')+'</div>'}
function profileHeatmap(){const names=['Age','Account Balance','Transaction Count','Activity Days','Transactions / 30 days','Financial Activity Score','Savings Account','Credit Card','Personal Loan','Investment Account','Digital Banking'],values=[[-1,.8,.8,0,-.9],[-.5,2,.1,.1,-1],[-1,1.8,.4,.1,-1.2],[-1.5,0,0,1.1,1.2],[1.8,-.1,0,-1,-1],[-.4,1.2,1,-1,-1.2],[-.5,1.1,-1,1.2,-1.4],[-1,.7,1.7,-.8,-.5],[-1,-1,1,-1,1.2],[-.7,2,0,-.6,-.6],[1.6,0,.2,-1.2,-1.3]],L=190,T=46,CW=77,RH=24,W=690,H=354;const color=v=>{const a=v<0?[55,125,226]:[240,111,82],t=Math.abs(v)/2,b=[22,41,60];return 'rgb('+b.map((x,i)=>Math.round(x+(a[i]-x)*t)).join(',')+')'},headers=['C0','C1','C2','C3','C4'].map((x,i)=>'<text x="'+(L+i*CW+CW/2)+'" y="32" text-anchor="middle" class="profile-heat-label">'+x+'</text>').join(''),rows=names.map((name,r)=>'<text x="'+(L-10)+'" y="'+(T+r*RH+16)+'" text-anchor="end" class="profile-heat-label">'+esc(name)+'</text>'+values[r].map((v,c)=>'<g><rect x="'+(L+c*CW)+'" y="'+(T+r*RH)+'" width="'+(CW-3)+'" height="'+(RH-3)+'" rx="4" fill="'+color(v)+'" class="profile-heat-cell"/><title>'+esc(name)+' · C'+c+' · approximate z-score '+v.toFixed(1)+'</title></g>').join('')).join(''),grad='<defs><linearGradient id="profile-heat-scale"><stop offset="0%" stop-color="#377de2"/><stop offset="50%" stop-color="#16293c"/><stop offset="100%" stop-color="#f06f52"/></linearGradient></defs>';return '<div class="profile-heatmap-wrap"><div class="profile-heatmap-title">Approximate standardized feature profile</div><svg class="profile-heatmap" viewBox="0 0 '+W+' '+H+'" role="img" aria-label="Approximate z-score heatmap of eleven features by five clusters">'+grad+headers+rows+'<rect x="'+L+'" y="323" width="'+(CW*5-3)+'" height="7" rx="4" fill="url(#profile-heat-scale)"/><text x="'+L+'" y="346" class="profile-heat-tick">−2 lower</text><text x="'+(L+CW*2.5)+'" y="346" text-anchor="middle" class="profile-heat-tick">0 overall</text><text x="'+(L+CW*5-3)+'" y="346" text-anchor="end" class="profile-heat-tick">+2 higher</text></svg><p class="source-note">Approximate values digitized from the supplied profile heatmap; hover a cell for its feature and cluster.</p></div>'}
function clusterScene(sizes,notes,selected){const colors=['#3b8cff','#ff9b42','#4fc783','#f05d64','#b476e6'],centers=[[325,250],[445,160],[570,250],[305,170],[420,295]],radii=[[112,73],[100,82],[115,80],[95,75],[90,62]],points=[];for(let i=0;i<sizes.length;i++){let seed=7919+i*1543;const rand=()=>{seed=(seed*16807)%2147483647;return(seed-1)/2147483646};for(let j=0;j<600;j++){const angle=rand()*Math.PI*2,r=Math.sqrt(rand()),x=centers[i][0]+Math.cos(angle)*r*radii[i][0],y=centers[i][1]+Math.sin(angle)*r*radii[i][1];points.push('<circle class="cluster-point" data-cluster-hover="'+i+'" cx="'+x.toFixed(1)+'" cy="'+y.toFixed(1)+'" r="2.4" fill="'+colors[i]+'" fill-opacity=".62" tabindex="0" role="button" aria-label="Cluster '+i+': '+fmt(sizes[i])+' customers"><title>Cluster '+i+' · '+fmt(sizes[i])+' customers · '+esc(notes[i])+'</title></circle>')}}const gridY=[80,150,220,290,360].map((y,i)=>'<line x1="65" y1="'+y+'" x2="780" y2="'+y+'" class="cluster-gridline"/><text x="52" y="'+(y+4)+'" class="cluster-axis-tick" text-anchor="end">'+(4-i*2)+'</text>').join(''),gridX=[100,235,370,505,640,775].map((x,i)=>'<line x1="'+x+'" y1="55" x2="'+x+'" y2="375" class="cluster-gridline"/><text x="'+x+'" y="396" class="cluster-axis-tick" text-anchor="middle">'+(-5+i*2)+'</text>').join(''),hulls=centers.map((c,i)=>'<ellipse cx="'+c[0]+'" cy="'+c[1]+'" rx="'+radii[i][0]+'" ry="'+radii[i][1]+'" fill="'+colors[i]+'" fill-opacity=".08" stroke="'+colors[i]+'" stroke-opacity=".8" stroke-width="1.5"/>').join(''),legend=colors.map((c,i)=>'<span style="--cluster-dot:'+c+'">C'+i+'</span>').join('');return '<div class="cluster-map-wrap"><div class="cluster-map-stage"><svg class="cluster-map" viewBox="0 0 820 430" role="img" aria-label="Illustrative 2D PCA-style map of five clusters; hover points for cluster details"><g>'+gridY+gridX+'</g>'+hulls+'<g>'+points.join('')+'</g><text x="420" y="421" text-anchor="middle" class="cluster-axis-label">PC1 · illustrative projection</text><text x="17" y="215" text-anchor="middle" class="cluster-axis-label" transform="rotate(-90 17 215)">PC2 · illustrative projection</text></svg><div class="cluster-map-tip" role="status"></div></div><div class="cluster-map-legend">'+legend+'</div></div><p class="source-note">Hover any point for its reported cluster size and profile; click a point to select it. The project includes cluster counts and profile notes, but not PCA coordinates or customer-level assignments, so the point layout is illustrative.</p>'}
async function clustering(){let [bench,out]=await Promise.all([api('/mining/benchmarks'),api('/mining/results')]),sizes=bench.clustering.sizes,labels=sizes.map((_,i)=>`Cluster ${i}`),current=sizes[cluster]||sizes[0],note=out.clustering.profileNotes[cluster];return `${head('Customer Segmentation','Explore the five-cluster solution, cluster profiles, and K-selection evidence.','K-MEANS')}<div class="notice"><strong>Feature treatment:</strong> money-valued fields were log1p transformed before standardization. The project result reports K-Means with n_init=10 and random_state=42, silhouette on a 3,000-customer sample, and K=5 chosen for separation and interpretability.</div><div class="grid kpis" style="margin-top:16px">${kpi('SELECTED K','5','Project clustering result')}${kpi('CLUSTER',`C${cluster}`,labels[cluster])}${kpi('CUSTOMERS',fmt(current),'Reported cluster size')}${kpi('SHARE',pct(current/summary.customers),'Of 20,000 customers')}</div><div class="grid cluster-top-grid" style="margin-bottom:16px">${card('K selection evidence','K = 2 through 7 · chart-digitized values are approximate',`<div class="k-selection-charts"><div><div class="card-sub">Approximate inertia</div>${chartBars(out.clustering.kValues.map((k,i)=>({name:`K=${k}`,value:out.clustering.inertiaApprox[i]})),{key:'name',value:'value',height:180,color:'#3989f3'})}</div><div><div class="card-sub">Approximate silhouette</div>${chartBars(out.clustering.kValues.map((k,i)=>({name:`K=${k}`,value:out.clustering.silhouetteApprox[i]})),{key:'name',value:'value',height:180,color:'#29b5c7',format:v=>Number(v).toFixed(3)})}</div></div><p class="source-note">Curve values are approximate; K=5 is retained as a practical choice balancing separation and interpretability. K=5 is a practical choice, not the maximum silhouette.</p>`)}${card('Cluster size distribution','Exact benchmark counts from the project results',chartBars(sizes.map((v,i)=>({name:`C${i}`,value:v})),{key:'name',value:'value',color:'#478fed'}))}</div><div class="grid cols2" style="margin-bottom:16px">${card('PCA Cluster map','Hover a point for cluster details; click to select',clusterSelector(sizes,cluster)+clusterScene(sizes,out.clustering.profileNotes,cluster))}${card('Mean profile by cluster','Approximate standardized feature comparison across C0–C4',`<div class="metric-band"><div class="metric"><b>${fmt(current)}</b><small>Customers</small></div><div class="metric"><b>${pct(current/summary.customers)}</b><small>Cluster share</small></div></div><div class="callout" style="margin-top:14px">${esc(note)}</div>${profileHeatmap()}<p class="source-note">Underlying z-scores are not included in the project files; these values are approximate readings from the supplied profile chart.</p>`)} </div>${card('Feature set','Clustering input dimensions',`<div class="detail-list">${out.clustering.features.map(f=>`<span class="pill">${esc(cap(f))}</span>`).join('')}</div><p class="footnote">Log1p is applied to skewed money-valued inputs before standard scaling. K=5 is retained as the established project output.</p>`) }`}
async function association(){let data=await api('/association/rules?support='+associationThreshold.support+'&confidence='+associationThreshold.confidence);let rr=data.rules.map(r=>({a:cap(r.antecedent),b:cap(r.consequent),...r}));window.currentRules=rr;return `${head('Association Rules','Explore co-occurrence patterns among five derived product-ownership indicators.','MARKET BASKET ANALYSIS')}<div class="notice"><strong>Definitions:</strong> Support is the frequency of an item combination. Confidence is the probability of B given A. Lift compares that probability with B’s baseline; lift &gt; 1 indicates positive co-occurrence, not causation.</div><div class="rule-highlight" style="margin:15px 0"><b>Strongest project benchmark · Personal Loan → Credit Card</b><div class="metric-band" style="margin-top:12px"><div class="metric"><b>0.166</b><small>Support</small></div><div class="metric"><b>0.577</b><small>Confidence</small></div><div class="metric"><b>1.884</b><small>Lift</small></div></div><p class="footnote">Benchmark statement: personal-loan customers are about 1.88× as likely to also have a credit card as the baseline rate. Product co-occurrence does not prove causation.</p></div><div class="toolbar"><label class="inline-label">Minimum support</label><input id="min-support" class="input" type="number" min="0" max="1" step=".01" value="${associationThreshold.support}"><label class="inline-label">Minimum confidence</label><input id="min-confidence" class="input" type="number" min="0" max="1" step=".01" value="${associationThreshold.confidence}"><button class="btn primary" id="apply-rules">Apply thresholds</button><input id="rule-search" class="input search" placeholder="Search product names"></div><div class="grid cols2" style="margin-bottom:16px">${card('Support & confidence','Actual values calculated from customer ownership flags',chartBars(rr.slice(0,8).map(r=>({name:`${r.a} → ${r.b}`,value:r.confidence})),{key:'name',value:'value',format:v=>pct(v)}))}${card('Lift by rule','Actual directional pairwise rule calculations',chartBars(rr.slice(0,8).map(r=>({name:`${r.a} → ${r.b}`,value:r.lift})),{key:'name',value:'value',color:'#1ba4b5',format:v=>Number(v).toFixed(2)}))}</div>${card('Rules table','Calculated from 20,000 customers · min support ${associationThreshold.support} · min confidence ${associationThreshold.confidence}',`<div id="rules-table">${rulesTable(rr)}</div>`)}<div class="spacer"></div>${card('Association parameters','',`<div class="metric-band"><div class="metric"><b>0.10</b><small>Minimum support</small></div><div class="metric"><b>0.50</b><small>Minimum confidence</small></div><div class="metric"><b>${fmt(summary.customers)}</b><small>Customer transactions</small></div><div class="metric"><b>5</b><small>Derived product indicators</small></div></div><p class="footnote">Association rules express patterns in the project’s derived product ownership flags. They do not establish customer intent or causation.</p>`)}`}
let ruleSort='lift',ruleDir=-1;
function rulesTable(rr){let sorted=[...rr].sort((a,b)=>{let x=ruleSort==='antecedent'?a.a:ruleSort==='consequent'?a.b:a[ruleSort],y=ruleSort==='antecedent'?b.a:ruleSort==='consequent'?b.b:b[ruleSort];return (x<y?-1:x>y?1:0)*ruleDir});return table(['<span class="sort-rule" data-sort-rule="antecedent">Antecedent ↕</span>','<span class="sort-rule" data-sort-rule="consequent">Consequent ↕</span>','<span class="sort-rule" data-sort-rule="support">Support ↕</span>','<span class="sort-rule" data-sort-rule="confidence">Confidence ↕</span>','<span class="sort-rule" data-sort-rule="lift">Lift ↕</span>'],sorted.map(r=>`<tr><td>${esc(r.a)}</td><td>${esc(r.b)}</td><td>${pct(r.support)}</td><td>${pct(r.confidence)}</td><td>${Number(r.lift).toFixed(3)}</td></tr>`).join(''))}
function associationScatter(rr){let W=620,H=260,L=62,R=22,T=18,B=44,x=v=>L+(W-L-R)*v/.22,y=v=>H-B-(H-T-B)*v/.8,maxLift=Math.max(1,...rr.map(r=>r.lift));return `<svg class="chart association-scatter" viewBox="0 0 ${W} ${H}" role="img" aria-label="Association rule support versus confidence bubble chart"><line x1="${L}" y1="${T}" x2="${L}" y2="${H-B}" stroke="#6f89a1"/><line x1="${L}" y1="${H-B}" x2="${W-R}" y2="${H-B}" stroke="#6f89a1"/><text x="${(L+W-R)/2}" y="${H-8}" text-anchor="middle">Support</text><text x="15" y="${(T+H-B)/2}" transform="rotate(-90 15 ${(T+H-B)/2})" text-anchor="middle">Confidence</text>${[0,.05,.1,.15,.2].map(v=>`<line x1="${x(v)}" y1="${T}" x2="${x(v)}" y2="${H-B}" stroke="#29445c" stroke-dasharray="3 5"/><text x="${x(v)}" y="${H-B+17}" text-anchor="middle">${v.toFixed(2)}</text>`).join('')}${[0,.2,.4,.6,.8].map(v=>`<line x1="${L}" y1="${y(v)}" x2="${W-R}" y2="${y(v)}" stroke="#29445c" stroke-dasharray="3 5"/><text x="${L-8}" y="${y(v)+3}" text-anchor="end">${v.toFixed(1)}</text>`).join('')}${rr.map(r=>`<circle cx="${x(r.support)}" cy="${y(r.confidence)}" r="${4+8*r.lift/maxLift}" fill="#45c3d0" fill-opacity=".72" stroke="#c4f2f5" stroke-opacity=".65"><title>${esc(r.a)} → ${esc(r.b)} | support ${r.support.toFixed(3)} | confidence ${r.confidence.toFixed(3)} | lift ${r.lift.toFixed(2)}</title></circle>`).join('')}</svg>`}function networkMarkup(){const nodes=[['Savings_Account',95,68],['Credit_Card',300,40],['Personal_Loan',505,68],['Investment_Account',160,158],['Digital_Banking',430,158]],pos=Object.fromEntries(nodes.map(n=>[n[0],[n[1],n[2]]]));let edges=(window.currentRules||[]).filter(r=>r.lift>1).slice(0,9);return `<section class="card" style="margin:16px 0"><div class="card-head"><div><div class="card-title">Product relationship network</div><div class="card-sub">Directed connections show rules meeting the current support and confidence thresholds; line strength follows lift.</div></div><span class="tag">${edges.length} relationships</span></div><svg class="network" viewBox="0 0 600 205" role="img" aria-label="Product association network">${edges.map(r=>{let a=pos[r.antecedent],b=pos[r.consequent];if(!a||!b)return '';return `<line x1="${a[0]}" y1="${a[1]}" x2="${b[0]}" y2="${b[1]}" stroke="#5c9bd4" stroke-width="${Math.min(4,1+r.lift)}" opacity=".45" marker-end="url(#arrow)"/>`}).join('')}<defs><marker id="arrow" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" refX="7" refY="3" orient="auto"><path d="M0,0 L0,6 L8,3 z" fill="#5c9bd4"/></marker></defs>${nodes.map(([n,x,y])=>`<g><circle cx="${x}" cy="${y}" r="24" fill="#eaf3ff" stroke="#4c8dd1"/><text x="${x}" y="${y+3}" text-anchor="middle" font-size="8" fill="#28557e">${esc(cap(n).split(' ').map(x=>x[0]).join(''))}</text><text x="${x}" y="${y+39}" text-anchor="middle" font-size="9" fill="#64788d">${esc(cap(n))}</text></g>`).join('')}</svg><div class="legend"><span style="--dot:#4c8dd1">Positive co-occurrence (lift &gt; 1)</span></div></section>`}
function bindPage(){if(page==='Dataset'){let input=$('#sample-search');input?.addEventListener('input',e=>{sampleSearch=e.target.value;samplePage=1;clearTimeout(window._st);window._st=setTimeout(render,250)});$('#prev')?.addEventListener('click',()=>{if(samplePage>1){samplePage--;render()}});$('#next')?.addEventListener('click',()=>{if(samplePage*sampleSize<sampleTotal){samplePage++;render()}});$('#sample-size')?.addEventListener('change',e=>{sampleSize=Number(e.target.value)||12;samplePage=1;render()});document.querySelectorAll('[data-sort]').forEach(x=>x.addEventListener('click',()=>{if(sampleSort===x.dataset.sort)sampleDir=sampleDir==='asc'?'desc':'asc';else{sampleSort=x.dataset.sort;sampleDir='asc'}render()}))}
if(page==='Data Warehouse'){document.querySelectorAll('[data-table]').forEach(x=>{x.onclick=()=>{activeTable=x.dataset.table;render()};x.onkeydown=e=>{if(e.key==='Enter'||e.key===' '){e.preventDefault();activeTable=x.dataset.table;render()}}});const scene=$('.schema-scene'),schema=$('.schema');scene?.addEventListener('pointermove',e=>{if(innerWidth<760)return;let r=scene.getBoundingClientRect(),x=(e.clientX-r.left)/r.width-.5,y=(e.clientY-r.top)/r.height-.5;schema.style.transform=`rotateX(${(-y*4).toFixed(2)}deg) rotateY(${(x*5).toFixed(2)}deg)`});scene?.addEventListener('pointerleave',()=>{if(schema)schema.style.transform='rotateX(0) rotateY(0)'})}
if(page==='OLAP Analysis'){['olap-mode','olap-level','olap-gender','olap-location','olap-fit','olap-year'].forEach(id=>$('#'+id)?.addEventListener('change',()=>{olapState[id.replace('olap-','')]= $('#'+id).value;if(id==='olap-level'||id==='olap-mode')olapState.period='';render()}));['pivot-rows','pivot-cols','pivot-measure'].forEach(id=>$('#'+id)?.addEventListener('change',()=>{olapState[{ 'pivot-rows':'rows','pivot-cols':'cols','pivot-measure':'measure'}[id]]=$('#'+id).value}));$('#olap-reset')?.addEventListener('click',()=>{Object.assign(olapState,{mode:'rollup',level:'month',gender:'',location:'',fit:'',year:'',period:'',rows:'Product_Fit_Category',cols:'Next_Product_Uptake',measure:'customers'});render()});$('#run-pivot')?.addEventListener('click',()=>{olapState.mode='pivot';olapState.period='';render()});document.querySelectorAll('[data-period]').forEach(el=>el.addEventListener('click',()=>{const next={year:'quarter',quarter:'month',month:'day'}[olapState.level];if(next){olapState.period=el.dataset.period;olapState.level=next;olapState.mode='drilldown';render()}}))}
if(page==='Classification'||page==='Next Product Prediction'){$('#find-customer')?.addEventListener('click',findCustomer);$('#customer-id')?.addEventListener('keydown',e=>{if(e.key==='Enter')findCustomer()})}
if(page==='Customer Segmentation'){const stage=$('.cluster-map-stage'),tip=$('.cluster-map-tip');stage?.addEventListener('pointerover',e=>{const point=e.target.closest('[data-cluster-hover]');if(!point||!tip)return;tip.innerHTML='<b>'+esc(point.querySelector('title')?.textContent||'')+'</b>';tip.classList.add('visible')});stage?.addEventListener('pointermove',e=>{if(!tip?.classList.contains('visible'))return;const r=stage.getBoundingClientRect();tip.style.left=Math.min(r.width-230,Math.max(8,e.clientX-r.left+14))+'px';tip.style.top=Math.max(8,e.clientY-r.top-12)+'px'});stage?.addEventListener('pointerleave',()=>tip?.classList.remove('visible'));document.querySelectorAll('[data-cluster-hover],[data-cluster]').forEach(x=>x.addEventListener('click',()=>{cluster=+(x.dataset.clusterHover??x.dataset.cluster);render()}))}if(page==='Association Rules'){$('#apply-rules')?.addEventListener('click',()=>{associationThreshold.support=Number($('#min-support').value)||0.10;associationThreshold.confidence=Number($('#min-confidence').value)||0.50;render()});$('#rule-search')?.addEventListener('input',e=>document.querySelectorAll('#rules-table tbody tr').forEach(tr=>tr.classList.toggle('hidden',!tr.textContent.toLowerCase().includes(e.target.value.toLowerCase()))));document.querySelectorAll('[data-sort-rule]').forEach(el=>el.addEventListener('click',()=>{if(ruleSort===el.dataset.sortRule)ruleDir*=-1;else{ruleSort=el.dataset.sortRule;ruleDir=-1}$('#rules-table').innerHTML=rulesTable(window.currentRules||[]);let q=$('#rule-search').value.toLowerCase();document.querySelectorAll('#rules-table tbody tr').forEach(tr=>tr.classList.toggle('hidden',!tr.textContent.toLowerCase().includes(q)))}))}}
async function findCustomer(){let result=$('#customer-result');try{let {customer:r,lastTransactionDate}=await api('/customer?id='+encodeURIComponent($('#customer-id').value.trim()));selectedCustomer=r;let products=[['Savings_Account','Savings Account'],['Credit_Card','Credit Card'],['Personal_Loan','Personal Loan'],['Investment_Account','Investment Account'],['Digital_Banking','Digital Banking']].filter(([k])=>+r[k]).map(x=>x[1]);result.innerHTML=`<div class="customer-card">${[['Customer ID',r.CustomerID],['Age / gender',`${r.Age} · ${r.CustGender}`],['Location',r.CustLocation],['Account balance',money(r.Account_Balance)],['Transaction count',fmt(r.Transaction_Count)],['Total transaction amount',money(r.Total_Transaction_Amount_INR)],['Average transaction amount',money(r.Average_Transaction_Amount_INR)],['Activity days',fmt(r.Activity_Days)],['Financial activity score',Number(r.Financial_Activity_Score).toFixed(3)],['Last source transaction',lastTransactionDate||'Not found'],['Current products',products.join(', ')||'None flagged'],['Product Fit Category',r.Product_Fit_Category],['Next Product Uptake',r.Next_Product_Uptake]].map(([a,b])=>`<div class="customer-field"><small>${a}</small><b>${esc(b)}</b></div>`).join('')}</div><p class="footnote">The displayed target labels are those recorded in the cleaned analytical CSV. No fitted model file was supplied, so this lookup is not represented as a new model prediction.</p>`}catch(e){result.innerHTML=`<div class="notice">${esc(e.message)}</div>`}}
async function runPivot(){let q=new URLSearchParams({rows:$('#pivot-rows').value,cols:$('#pivot-cols').value,measure:$('#pivot-measure').value});try{let p=await api('/olap/pivot?'+q),el=$('#pivot-result');el.innerHTML=`<div class="card-sub" style="margin:10px 0">${esc(p.operation)} · ${esc(p.rowDimension)} × ${esc(p.columnDimension)} · ${fmt(p.summary.customers)} customers</div>${table(['Row',...p.columns].map(esc),p.rows.map(r=>`<tr><td>${esc(r.row)}</td>${p.columns.map(c=>`<td>${fmt(r[c],1)}</td>`).join('')}</tr>`).join(''))}` }catch(e){$('#pivot-result').textContent=e.message}}
function boot(){let nav=$('#nav');nav.innerHTML=navItems.map(([n,i])=>`<button data-page="${n}" data-tooltip="${n}" aria-label="${n}" class="${n===page?'active':''}"><span class="nav-icon">${i}</span><span class="nav-label">${n}</span></button>`).join('');nav.addEventListener('click',e=>{let b=e.target.closest('[data-page]');if(b){page=b.dataset.page;render();$('#sidebar').classList.remove('open')}});$('#menu').onclick=()=>{if(innerWidth<=760)$('#sidebar').classList.toggle('open');else $('#sidebar').classList.toggle('expanded')};render()}
if(location.protocol==='file:'){$('#app').innerHTML='<section class="card startup-card"><div class="eyebrow">LOCAL SERVER REQUIRED</div><h1 class="page-title">Start the dashboard server</h1><p class="page-sub">This page was opened from disk. The data APIs and interactive analysis need the local Node server.</p><div class="method-step" style="margin:18px 0"><b>From the project folder, run</b><code>node backend/server.js</code></div><p class="page-sub">Open the localhost URL printed in the terminal. If port 8000 is occupied, the server automatically tries another port.</p></section>'}else boot();


















